This release changes the Sync schema and MUST be applied through the cutover
workflow, not the ordinary main deploy.

The ordinary deploy runs migrate and recreate outside the cutover lock, with no
quiesce, no capacity gate, no pre-fingerprint and no verified rollback artifact.
For this release that is the exact path the cutover exists to prevent, so
`.github/scripts/hetzner-remote.sh` refuses to migrate while this file is
present. It refuses twice over: once on this file, which only exists in the
repository, and once on `cutover_required=yes` in the manifest delivered to the
app host out of this release's own worker image — the app host has no repository,
so the second check is the one that actually fires there.

RUN IT ON THE APP HOST, NOT FROM THE REPOSITORY

The wrapper is delivered by the deploy, not checked out. `prepare_runtime`
extracts it from `ghcr.io/erhanrdn/omniads-worker:<sha>` and installs it at:

  /var/www/adsecute/cutover/hetzner-sync-cutover.sh

alongside `cutover-wrapper.manifest`, which pins its SHA-256. The wrapper
re-hashes itself against that manifest before every phase and refuses if the two
disagree, so do not edit it in place — re-deliver it with:

  .github/scripts/hetzner-remote.sh deliver_cutover_wrapper

Apply, phase by phase, with DEPLOY_SHA set to the exact commit:

  preflight -> quiesce -> fingerprint-pre -> migrate -> verify-contract
            -> fingerprint-post -> deploy-disabled -> enable -> resume-scheduler

`preflight` takes a FRESH full backup on the database host, restores it into a
scratch database and binds the manifest to this database's system identifier —
it is not a grep of somebody else's manifest, and it will refuse if the artifact
cannot be restored. `emergency-disable` is always available and invalidates any
enable/resume proof, so a cutover that was stopped can only continue by
re-establishing the runtime proof with `deploy-disabled`.

Remove this file in the commit that follows a completed cutover, and re-run
`npm run cutover:package` so the delivered manifest stops saying
`cutover_required=yes`.
